          "text": "{\"schema_version\":\"ai-evaluator-v2/1.1\",\"case_id\":\"9-5\",\"candidate_id\":\"candidate_3\",\"action_assessment\":{\"status\":\"preserved\",\"summary\":\"The main business actions are present with acceptable meaning: receive report, conditionally create account, review, supervisor approval/rejection, rejection notice, reimbursement, progress email, cancellation notice, and resubmission requirement.\"},\"flow_assessment\":{\"status\":\"defect\",\"summary\":\"Core early ordering is preserved, but the required delayed-case progression is not: a request that exceeds 7 days should still be able to reach 30-day cancellation later, whereas the graph makes progress-email and cancellation outcomes mutually exclusive and routes the progress-email path to reimbursement.\"},\"control_flow_assessment\":{\"status\":\"defect\",\"summary\":\"The time-based logic is modeled incorrectly as one exclusive post-approval decision. The source requires cumulative escalation for unfinished requests: send an approval-in-progress email after 7 days and, if still unfinished by 30 days, stop the process and cancel; the graph cannot realize both in sequence.\"},\"main_error_type\":\"wrong_branching_or_condition\",\"explanation\":\"The source describes two time-triggered conditions over the same unfinished request: after 7 days the employee must receive an approval-in-progress email, and if the request is still unfinished within 30 days the process must stop with cancellation and resubmission. The generated graph instead places a single exclusive decision after approval with branches for completed_in_time, approval_in_progress, or cancelled. Because the approval-in-progress branch merges into reimbursement, a delayed request cannot later be cancelled after 30 days, and the 30-day case omits the required earlier progress notice. This materially changes the delay-handling behavior even though the main approval/rejection actions are otherwise captured.\",\"overall_score\":0.64,\"severity\":\"moderate\",\"confidence\":\"high\",\"ambiguity_flag\":false,\"ambiguity_explanation\":\"\",\"requires_human_review\":false,\"review_reason\":\"\"}"
        }
